ng yeast</td><td align="left" colspan="2">Fission yeast</td><td align="left" colspan="2">Fruit fly</td><td align="left" colspan="2">Nematode</td><td align="left" colspan="2"><italic>Arabidopsis</italic></td><td align="left" colspan="2">Human</td></tr><tr><td colspan="13"><hr></hr></td></tr><tr><td align="left">R<sub>Q/N </sub>(total residues)</td><td align="left">1.05</td><td></td><td align="left">2.28</td><td></td><td align="left">6.89</td><td></td><td align="left">6.96</td><td></td><td align="left">5.43</td><td></td><td align="left">7.09</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">R<sub>Q/N </sub>(total regions)</td><td align="left">1.42</td><td></td><td align="left">4.25</td><td></td><td align="left">5.03</td><td></td><td align="left">6.75</td><td></td><td align="left">5.46</td><td></td><td align="left">11.73</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Q/N (composition)</td><td align="left">(0.039/0.061) = 0.64</td><td></td><td align="left">(0.038/0. 052) = 0.73</td><td></td><td align="left">(0.052/0 .047) = 1.12</td><td></td><td align="left">(0.041/ 0.049 = 0.83</td><td></td><td align="left">(0.035/ 0.044 = 0.79</td><td></td><td align="left">(0.047/ 0.037 = 1.28</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p>*The total numbers of regions that have a compositional biased LPS with P<sub>bias </sub>&#x0003c; 1 &#x000d7; 10-13. <sup>&#x02020;</sup>The number of LPSs for a particular compositional bias in the budding yeast proteome that overlap a region assigned as coiled coil by the MULTICOIL program [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B22">22</xref>]. <sup>&#x02021;</sup>The total numbers of bias residues (for example, total number of serines for a serine bias) for all of the regions tallied for part (a) of the table. <sup>&#x000a7;</sup> R<sub>Q/N </sub>is the ratio of the number of Q-rich regions to N-rich regions as listed in parts (a) and (b) of the table. The overall abundance of the residues is simply the fraction of the total proteome that is either Q or N.</p></table-